#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# root

#% text
# `root(x => p(x), k)` stands for the `k`-th root of the polynomial `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The roots are ordered: the real roots ascending, then the complex roots by real part and then imaginary part.

#% item
# A `root` object is exact: it stays as it is and `n` evaluates it to any precision. `roots` and `solve` give `root` objects for factors without a solution in radicals.

#% item
# The canonical form: a root object prints with its polynomial as a slot function, `root(&(p(&1)), k)`, whatever variable it was written with; the polynomial is the primitive irreducible factor over the rationals that the root belongs to, and `k` its index among that factor's roots. A root of a factor of degree one is that rational number, of degree two the radical `(-b +- sqrt(b^2 - 4 a c))/(2 a)`.

#% item
# `root(f, k, 0)` is the same as `root(f, k)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
root(x => x^3 - 2, 1)
#% output
#= root(&(-2 + &1^3), 1)

#% cell
n(root(x => x^3 - 2, 1))
#% output
#= 1.2599210498948732

#% cell
n(root(x => x^5 - x + 1, 1), 30)
#% output
#= -1.1673039782614186842560458998548422

#% cell
n(root(x => x^5 - x + 1, 2))
#% output
#= -0.18123244446987535 - 1.0839541013177107im

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The roots of a quintic, in order:

#% cell
n(table(root(x => x^5 - 3*x + 1, k), k, 5))
#% output
#= [-1.3887919844072543, 0.3347341419433527, 1.2146480426984618, -0.08029510011728015 - 1.328355109820654im, -0.08029510011728015 + 1.328355109820654im]

#% text
# Roots of reducible polynomials and of quadratics:

#% cell
root(&(&1^5 - 3*&1), 2)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
root(&(&1^2 - 3*&1 - 1), 2)
#% output
#= (1/2)*(3 + 13^(1/2))

#% cell
root(&(&1^5 - 3*&1), 3)
#% output
#= root(&(-3 + &1^4), 2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The value is a root:

#% cell
r = n(root(x => x^5 - x + 1, 1)); r^5 - r + 1
#% output
#= -6.661338147750939e-16

#% text
# `solve` returns `root` objects:

#% cell
solve(x^5 - x + 1 == 0, x)[1]
#% output
#= [x -> root(&(1 - &1 + &1^5), 1)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `roots`, `solve`, `n`, `find_root`
